---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pricing — how lesson prices work | LearnNest" description="How LearnNest pricing works: each tutor sets their own price, trials are 25 or 50 minutes, and lesson packs run for 28 days. Demo prices only." path="/pricing">
  <h1>Pricing — simple and clear</h1>
  <p class="lede">There is no single LearnNest price. Each tutor sets their own price for a 50-minute lesson, and you choose how often you want to learn.</p>
  <p class="demo-note"><strong>Demo prices:</strong> all prices on this page are samples. No payment is taken on this demo site.</p>

  <h2>How a lesson is priced</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Each tutor sets their own price.</strong> In this demo, sample prices run from $8 to $45 per 50-minute lesson.</li>
    <li><strong>A trial is 25 or 50 minutes.</strong> A 25-minute trial costs half the 50-minute price. For example, a tutor charging $20 for 50 minutes charges $10 for a 25-minute trial.</li>
    <li><strong>You pay per tutor, not per site.</strong> If you learn with two tutors, each one has their own price and their own lesson pack.</li>
    <li><strong>No hidden fees in the demo.</strong> The price you see on a tutor’s profile is the price used in the example below.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Lesson packs — an example</h2>
  <p>This table is an <strong>example only</strong>, using a sample tutor who charges <strong>$20 per 50-minute lesson</strong>. Your total depends on the tutor you choose.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Pack</th><th>Lessons per 28 days</th><th>Example total at $20 / lesson</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Starter</strong></td><td>4 lessons</td><td>$80</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Regular</strong></td><td>8 lessons</td><td>$160</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Intensive</strong></td><td>12 lessons</td><td>$240</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="meta">Example maths: 4 × $20 = $80; 8 × $20 = $160; 12 × $20 = $240. A tutor charging $12 would cost $48, $96 and $144 for the same packs.</p>

  <h2>What if a tutor is not right for you?</h2>
  <p>Try a trial with a different tutor. In a real marketplace, a trial that does not work out can be replaced; on this demo, booking a trial only shows a confirmation on the page and nothing is charged.</p>

  <h2>Can I pause or cancel?</h2>
  <p>In a real marketplace you could pause a pack or cancel before the next 28-day period starts. On this demo there is no account, no subscription and nothing to cancel.</p>

  <p><a class="btn" href="/tutors">Browse tutors and prices →</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
